< The checkpoints are Phi-4-mini-reasoning, Qwen3-4B, Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-14B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-\allowbreak Llama-8B and Granite-3.2-8B-Instruct with its reasoning mode on \cite{microsoft2025phireasoning,yang2025qwen3,guo2025deepseek,ibmgranite2025}. For each budget $c\in\{0,64,128,\allowbreak 256,512,768\}$ we force exactly $c$ reasoning tokens by suppressing end-of-sequence, then append an answer prompt and take the most likely option letter; the free-text answer is also recorded. The prompt lists the options in randomized order, gives the objective as ``(private value $-$ b) $\times$ estimated win probability'' and asks the model not to infer the answer from option position. Greedy decoding runs under three option orders per scenario (648 decisions per model and budget); five sampled seeds run at three budgets; a run without forcing lets each model stop within 1{,}024 tokens. A 768-token decision takes 9--35 seconds and costs under one cent at RunPod rates \cite{runpod2026pricing}. A synthetic version with exact payoffs \cite{krishna2010auction} uses the same protocol.
